  "caveats": [
    "A simulation with chosen, not estimated, parameters: results describe the simulator.",
    "The crisis regime is an exogenous random switch; bail-outs cannot change how often crises start, only what they do to banks and output.",
    "Firms are one aggregate leverage ratio, the government one budget, the foreign sector one exchange rate; no sectoral detail, no trade partners, no default on sovereign debt.",
    "Bank rescue is mechanical (inject up to a target ratio); real rescues involve negotiation, conditionality and political limits."
  ]
